@0    = ~I am curious about something, <CHARNAME>, why did you pick me up for your merry band of misfits?~
@1    = ~I thought we needed another good fighter in our group.~
@2    = ~Well, I guess the thought of a warlord would make a good addition to our group of "misfits".~
@3    = ~I'd rather not talk about it right now.~
@4    = ~I like the idea of a crazy, bloodthirsty elf in my group.~
@5    = ~A good fighter? Ah yes I am very good with a sword. I love to dive into the middle of a battle, hacking away at all of those in my sight. Feel their blood splatter on my body. It's invigorating!~
@6    = ~Uh yeah. I think we should be going now.~
@7    = ~What a refreshing insight you have, Callisto. I feel the same way about battle myself.~
@8    = ~An odd insight you have there, Callisto. Battle is for honor, not for the sake of bloodshed.~
@9    = ~To each their own I suppose. Whatever it takes to win I guess. Glad that you are on our side.~
@10   = ~Glad to hear it, <CHARNAME>. It would appear we have something in common, which fills me with joy!~
@11   = ~Now, now don't you go and get preachy with me. Save it for someone who would care to hear it!~
@12   = ~We may have something in common yet. Stick with me, <CHARNAME> and I will teach you what I know about fighting.~
@13   = ~"Knowledge is power and power is through knowledge" was something I learned at Candlekeep.~
@14   = ~Well, you show signs of intelligence after all, <CHARNAME>. Having someone in the group with my skills can only benefit you in the long run. Plus it serves me just as well.~
@15   = ~Serves you? What do you mean?~
@16   = ~Oh my little dumpling don't read too much in to it. I only meant that it benefits me because I'm not stuck in a tavern in a dull city. I prefer being out in the open and sight seeing.~
@17   = ~For some reason I don't believe you.~
@18   = ~Yeah I prefer being out of the city myself. I understand.~
@19   = ~Good.~
@20   = ~So be it!~
@21   = ~(Callisto says nothing but smiles at you, making you feel uneasy.)~
@22   = ~Tell me something about yourself, <CHARNAME>. I wish to know more about you, our glorious leader that I follow!~
@23   = ~Why do you want to know?~
@24   = ~I was raised in Candlekeep by monks. It's not really exciting.~
@25   = ~Alas I am but a simple <PRO_RACE> making their way through the world.~
@26   = ~Well, <CHARNAME> my sweet, I wish to know more about my faithful, fearless leader. Nothing more.~
@27   = ~I was raised in Candlekeep by monks. My life story is not really exciting.~
@28   = ~Candlekeep, that fortified library? Sounds dull if you ask me, <CHARNAME>. Spending your days and nights with your nose stuck in all those books.~
@29   = ~Yes it was dull, reading all of those books. It's one reason why I am no longer there and free to travel the Sword Coast.~
@30   = ~I would not call it dull by any means, Callisto. I learned a lot with my "nose" stuck in the books.~
@31   = ~Candlekeep was a good place to be raised. I learned much from the books I read and what my instructors taught me. If it was not for that knowledge, I may not be where I am today.~
@32   = ~You surprise me, <CHARNAME>, knowledge is not a trivial thing to be caste aside. It can give you power, power over others who would seek to do you harm. Always keep an open mind and learn all that you can learn. Remember that.~
@33   = ~Good <CHARNAME>, good to hear that. Knowledge is power, power over others who would seek to do you harm. Always keep an open mind and learn all that you can learn. Remember that.~
@34   = ~Good <CHARNAME>, good to hear that my pet. Keep in mind that knowledge is power, power over others who would seek to do you harm. Always keep an open mind and learn all that you can learn. Remember that.~
@35   = ~A simple <PRO_RACE>, <CHARNAME>? You are much too modest. I think you are much more than that, much, much more.~
@36   = ~Well I was raised in Candlekeep by monks. It's not really an exciting story to tell.~
@37   = ~I was wondering, <CHARNAME>, do you have any family?~
@38   = ~None that I would consider relatives.~
@39   = ~Yes I have quite a few from what I have heard.~
@40   = ~The only relatives I have is Imoen.~
@41   = ~Always so nosey, Calli? I prefer not to talk about.~
@42   = ~What do you mean by that, <CHARNAME>?~
@43   = ~You could say that all the Bhaalspawn are my siblings, in a way.~
@44   = ~Never mind. I don't like talking about it.~
@45   = ~Bhaal is my father and had many offspring but I don't consider them family.~
@46   = ~Very well.~
@47   = ~Oh really? I find this interesting.~
@48   = ~If you say so. What about you?~
@49   = ~So, Calli, what about your family? Are any of them still alive?~
@50   = ~I'd rather hear about your family.~
@51   = ~Me? I don't know if I should tell you.~
@52   = ~Come now, Calli, you can tell me.~
@53   = ~Calli, I am interested in learning about you. You can tell me, please.~
@54   = ~My family is dead. Dead, dead, dead... (She falls silent and stares off into the distance.)~
@55   = ~What is it, Callisto, what happened to them?~
@56   = ~What's wrong Calli?~
@57   = ~No, I have no family. They died when a band of raiders attacked my village. They slaughtered everyone including my parents and my sisters. A few young children were taken to be sold as slaves.~
@58   = ~They scarred me and left me for dead. Left buried underneath the corpses of the villagers. Buried alive, buried alive...~
@59   = ~Now I hunt down all of those who were responsible. I'll KILL THEM ALL! And if anyone stands in my way, they will die as well!~
@60   = ~Many years ago I had a family, now, no longer. They died when a band of raiders attacked my village. They slaughtered everyone including my parents and my sisters. A few young children were taken to be sold as slaves.~
@61   = ~What is it, <CHARNAME>, something on your mind?~
@62   = ~I find your wanton killing disturbing especially when it concerns innocent bystanders.~
@63   = ~I find it refreshing to have someone who shares my lust for bloodshed.~
@64   = ~It's nothing. We should get going.~
@65   = ~Do you have a conscience? Your wanton killing is very disturbing, Callisto.~
@66   = ~Oh? Am I supposed to care? If people are stupid enough to get in my way, they'll get what's coming to them.~
@67   = ~Well I care and you better watch your actions in the future if you wish to travel with me.~
@68   = ~From now on I want you to be careful. You're in my party and I will not have needless bloodshed being spilt.~
@69   = ~(Callisto glares at you for a moment then smiles.) We'll see.~
@70   = ~I will consider it just for you, <CHARNAME>. For now.~
@71   = ~Oh really? I am glad you approve. Wanton carnage can go a long way into striking fear into your enemies.~
@72   = ~So be it.~ [cmca33]
@73   = ~A conscience? At one time I may have had one but not any more. It died in the fires of my village as it was put to the flames by those raiders.~
@74   = ~Why should my so called wanton killing disturb you? You have much blood on your hands, <CHARNAME>.~
@75   = ~That may be true but that is from defending myself. I don't kill senselessly.~
@76   = ~Yes that is true and I regret most of it. Taking another's life is a horrible action to do.~
@77   = ~Save me your sanctimonious mumbo jumbo. You're the offspring of the god of murder. Murder and killing is in your very blood. Bah! This discussion bores me, leave me!~
@78   = ~You're weak, <CHARNAME>. The blood of Bhaal is wasted in you. Leave me, I tire of this conversation!~
@79   = ~Such a pretty day for a blood bath, heh, heh!~ [cmca36]
@80   = ~Are psychotic urges all that drive you, Calli?~
@81   = ~That it is. I like the way you think, Calli.~
@82   = ~You have a weird sense of humor, Calli.~
@83   = ~Calli, you have a strange sense of what is beautiful.~
@84   = ~Why do you ask?~
@85   = ~Isn't there anything else you want to do in your life besides seeking revenge? Settle down, have a family?~
@86   = ~Revenge isn't everything, Calli. Having a family, doing something with your life is something you could look forward to doing.~
@87   = ~Revenge is a cold lonely path to take. Don't you want to do something with your life like have a family?~
@88   = ~You can't be filled with hatred the rest of your life. Ever think about atonement for your crimes?~
@89   = ~Thank you.~
@90   = ~Oh no, no, no, <CHARNAME>, you have it all wrong. I was not making a joke, I was very serious.~
@91   = ~I enjoy your blood thirsty presence in the group Calli.~
@92   = ~Pretty. Oh yes very pretty. Now what's really on your mind, <CHARNAME>?~ [cmca23]
@93   = ~You know, revenge isn't everything, Calli. Falling in love, starting a family, doing something with your life is something you could look forward to.~
@94   = ~I will spend eternity seeking revenge! No love, no family, nothing! I care for nothing but to see my family avenged!~ [cmca37]
@95   = ~Carrying all of that hate will poison your soul and destroy you in the end, Callisto. Do you think your family would want to see that happen to you?~
@96   = ~Do you think your family would want you to be on this path of vengeance? Do you?~
@97   = ~You know nothing of my family! NOTHING! Leave me! I have nothing else to say!~
@98   = ~I have no use for such things, <CHARNAME>. Revenge is all I need, it burns within me as the fires that consumed my village where I was raised burned brightly.~
@99   = ~Burns brightly...~
@100  = ~Atonement? Atonement is for those who have committed a crime. I have committed no crime. My revenge is justified! JUSTIFIED! Justice will be swift and final to those who wronged me!~
@101  = ~That is not justice, Callisto. Don't mix up justice with revenge.~
@102  = ~(Callisto glares at you and says nothing more.)~
@103  = ~Same old torture everyday, everyday.~ [cmca38]
@104  = ~Is something wrong, Calli?~
@105  = ~Boredom getting to you?~
@106  = ~Could you keep your nonsense to yourself?~
@107  = ~Something wrong you ask? Why yes, I'm bored!~
@108  = ~Why not find a spider and pull its legs off to amuse yourself?~
@109  = ~Bored? Why not sharpen your sword or something?~
@110  = ~I really don't care. Go find something to amuse yourself with.~
@111  = ~It got to me a long time ago. Amuse me, <CHARNAME>!~
@112  = ~If you wish but I make no promises.~
@113  = ~How about finding some homeless person instead and pull their limbs off? That seems more satisfying than some stupid bug. But come to think of it, weak people are nothing but bugs that should be squashed.~
@114  = ~Sounds like a good idea to me, Calli, can I have some fun by participating?~
@115  = ~Is this your idea of a joke I hope?~
@116  = ~That is sick, Calli! I hope that was some perverse joke.~
@117  = ~Sure why not. I could probably teach you a thing or two in the finer points of draw and quartering.~
@118  = ~(Callisto smiles at you coldly.) Heh, we'll see.~
@119  = ~My sword never needs to be sharpen. It has magical properties that always ensure a nice razor sharp edge.~
@120  = ~(She runs her hand across the edge, cutting into her palm. She shows no sign pain as blood starts to trickle down her arm.) See, very sharp.~
@121  = ~Eh yeah I can see that its sharp. Didn't that hurt?~
@122  = ~Neat. No pain no gain right?~
@123  = ~You can turn off the tough girl act, that must have hurt.~
@124  = ~No it didn't hurt. A minor injury like this is nothing to me. I became immune to pain a long, long time ago. Thanks for curing me of my boredom by the way.~
@125  = ~Yes, you could say that. Minor pain like this, I became immune to a long time ago. Thanks for curing me of my boredom by the way.~
@126  = ~I could amuse myself by disemboweling you in your sleep and play around with your entrails.~
@127  = ~Oh don't look at me like that, I was just joking.~
@128  = ~(You notice Callisto looks tired this day. You thought you heard her screaming in her sleep the night before.)~
@129  = ~(You say nothing and go about your business.)~
@130  = ~Did you get much sleep? You look worn down.~
@131  = ~Hard night last night?~
@132  = ~Did you have a nightmare last night? I thought I heard you scream in your sleep.~
@133  = ~(Callisto yawns and goes about her business.)~
@134  = ~Hmmm? Oh, no, I didn't sleep well last night. Must be all of this traveling is starting to get to me.~
@135  = ~I thought you may have had a nightmare judging by the screaming in your sleep.~
@136  = ~Oh, I thought it might have been a guilty conscience starting to get to you.~
@137  = ~Sorry about all of the traveling we have done recently, but it is necessary for us right now.~
@138  = ~The way you were screaming in your sleep last night, I thought you had a nightmare that prevented you from having peaceful rest.~
@139  = ~Nightmare? Why would I have a nightmare? Are you trying to imply something, <CHARNAME>? If so speak your mind.~
@140  = ~Nothing at all. Not my business any way.~
@141  = ~Well if you are having nightmares, perhaps it may have had something to do with the tragedy you experienced when you were young.~
@142  = ~Having those nightmares, perhaps your conscience is starting to get to you.~
@143  = ~If you are having nightmares, it could be the result of your guilt surfacing from killing those people who never did anything to you.~
@144  = ~Conscience? Guilt? For what? Just because some dirt farmer and his family got in my way for harboring one of those villains who destroyed my village, I should feel guilty for slaughtering them? No, never!~
@145  = ~It's your conscience, you have to live with it not me.~
@146  = ~Good to hear. For a moment I thought you were getting weak. A guilty conscience is a weakness after all.~
@147  = ~You should talk about this, Calli, it will bring you peace if you do.~
@148  = ~Feeling sorry for what you have done and admitting your guilt will ease your conscience after all.~
@149  = ~(Callisto looks at you coldly and says nothing else.)~
@150  = ~(Callisto looks at you for a moment and turns away. She says nothing more on the subject.)~
@151  = ~(Her look of sadness is only brief, her facial features harden.) No. Not at all. I left that behind me a long time ago. I, I have nothing else to say!~
@152  = ~(She eyes you coldly.) Why should I be guilty? Just because some dirt farmer and his family got in my way for harboring one of those villains who destroyed my village, I should feel guilty for slaughtering them? No, never!~
@153  = ~Yes, <CHARNAME>, what is it?~
@154  = ~Sorry I bumped into you, I didn't need anything.~
@155  = ~I was wondering if you ever thought about being redeemed?.~
@156  = ~Have you ever thought about being redeemed and being a person who fights for the side of all that is good?~
@157  = ~So far your path has been one of vengeance and doing deeds of great evil. Have you ever thought that you may have been wrong in your choices and perhaps its time to turn your life around and seek redemption?~
@158  = ~So be it.~ [cmca33]
@159  = ~Redeemed? Redeemed for what?~
@160  = ~Redeemed for all of the crimes you've comitted, all the evil that you have done to others, that sort of thing.~
@161  = ~Well I thought since you have killed so many innocent people, you may feel guilty about it and wish to atone for your crimes.~
@162  = ~You've done great acts of evil, killed so many who didn't deserve it, I thought you may wish to atone for your crimes.~
@163  = ~Oh nothing. Continue on your current path, its perfect.~
@164  = ~Crimes? What crimes? Killing those who harbored my enemies who were responsible for the death of my village, they got what they deserved! They harbored and sheltered those guilty murderers, they became guilty themselves and my enemies! Those murderers made me and any blood that I have spilt is on their hands! You speak about redemption one more time, <CHARNAME>, and I'll end you!~
@165  = ~Guilty for what? I didn't kill any innocents, no not at all. Those fools who harbored those murderers and refused to surender them, they're guilty for the blood that was spilt when I destroyed their villages not me! Same goes with those murderers who destroyed my family, any blood I have spilt is on their hands as well! You speak of this again, <CHARNAME>, and I'll end you!~
@166  = ~Go away.~ [cmca39]
@167  = ~I haven't done any evil, I did what had to be done to achieve my vengeance and my choices were never wrong. And what is this talk of redemption, redemption for what?~
@168  = ~Redeemed for all of the crimes you've comitted, all the evil that you have done to others, that sort of evil acts that you have comitted.~
@169  = ~(You take notice that Callisto looks tired today, you heard her screaming, crying and pleading last night. You've noticed that her sleep lately has become very restless and her beautiful elven appearance is that of someone who is worn out and haggard.)~
@170  = ~Did you get much sleep last night? You look worn out and beat.~
@171  = ~I thought I heard you crying in your sleep last night, what was that about?~
@172  = ~Did you have a nightmare last night? I thought I heard you screaming, crying and pleading to someone in your sleep.~
@173  = ~(Callisto yawns and goes about her business. You notice her hands have a slight tremor to them.)~
@174  = ~What? Didn't we have a conversation like this before? Are you spying on me when I sleep?~
@175  = ~No, I'm not spying on you. I noticed you haven't been getting a good night's sleep and I was concerned about it.~
@176  = ~Well, my concern was that if you are not getting a good night's sleep you may make an error in judgement the next time we are in a fight. I can't very well have my best fighter making mistakes.~
@177  = ~Calm down I was not spying on you, its just an observation, nothing more.~
@178  = ~Worry not, <CHARNAME>, worry not at all. Everything is fine, it'll be so fine...~
@179  = ~That's what I keep telling myself and yet...~
@180  = ~Mistakes? I haven't made mistakes... oh no, no, not I! My judgement is intact and sound. I keep telling myself, I keep telling myself... I made no mistakes.~
@181  = ~Yet I doubt...~
@182  = ~Worry not, <CHARNAME>, worry not at all. Every thing is fine, it'll be so fine...~
@183  = ~Crying? What are you talking about, <CHARNAME>? Crying is for the weak and something I would never do! No, no...never...~
@184  = ~(Callisto gives you a crazed look.) What? What are you going on about, <CHARNAME>? I'm fine, never felt better!~
@185  = ~I-it is all right, it is all right there's nothing wrong, nothing wrong...~
@186  = ~Aaiiirrrghhhh!!~ [cmca11]
@187  = ~Is there something wrong, Callisto?~
@188  = ~Being on the road is starting to get to you, Callisto?~
@189  = ~What's going on? Are we under attack?~
@190  = ~(Callisto goes about her business, laughing, crying and talking to herself.)~
@191  = ~Same old torture every day, every day. Ha, ha!~ [cmca38]
@192  = ~I see them, see them in my waking hours now! Leave me alone! It's not my fault, NOT MY FAULT!~
@193  = ~(You grab a hold of Callisto's shoulders.) Oh it's you. N-nothing is wrong. La, la, la, I can't hear you. There I can't hear them now, <CHARNAME>, lets get going shall we?~ [cmca16]
@194  = ~(You grab a hold of Callisto's shoulders.) Oh it's you. Just a moment, <CHARNAME>. La, la, la, I can't hear you. There I can't hear them now, <CHARNAME>, lets get going shall we?~ [cmca16]
@195  = ~Attack? Where? Oh, <CHARNAME>, don't you be fooling around with me, we're not under attack. But I'm under attack!~
@196  = ~Ah, yes! What a wonderful smell, it smells like a battlefield! Rotting flesh and blood galore! Wonderful if you ask me.~
@197  = ~Same old torture every day, every day. HA! HA! HA! I can't take it any more!~ [cmca38]
@198  = ~Are we going off the deep end again today?~
@199  = ~I have to say that your mood swings are getting tiring.~
@200  = ~What is wrong now, Callisto?~
@201  = ~I can't go on living like this! The voices are driving me insane!~
@202  = ~Guilty conscience has finally got to you, is that it?~
@203  = ~Voices aye? I think this is where we depart company now.~
@204  = ~Well if you're this weak minded, then fall on your sword and be done with it.~
@205  = ~You should seek a healer, Callisto.~
@206  = ~(Callisto doesn't even acknowledge what you said to her.) Can't you hear them? The voices all around, night and day! I can hear them in my dreams, when I'm awake, I can't go on living any more!~
@207  = ~And you're going to help me end it! Draw your weapon! I'm going to die as a warrior!~
@208  = ~You really are insane. You want to fight *me*? Draw your sword and I'll end you.~
@209  = ~I-I don't want to fight you, Callisto. We can take you to a healer and help you out. We're friends remember? Friends!~
@210  = ~Sounds to me like you would rather die as a coward instead of confronting these "voices". So be it, steel yourself.~
@211  = ~I always thought you were a weak link, now you've proven it. Prepare to meet your end!~
@212  = ~HA! HA! HA! I have a better idea!~
@213  = ~Oh do tell.~
@214  = ~I see that wild look in your eyes. Surely we can talk this over.~
@215  = ~I know that look. Prepare yourself!~
@216  = ~Wrong? WRONG? Can't you hear them? The voices all around, night and day! I can hear them in my dreams, when I'm awake, I can't go on living any more!~
@217  = ~You really are insane. You want to fight *me*? Draw your sword and I'll end you!~
@218  = ~I-I don't want to fight you, Callisto. We can take you to a healer and help you out. We're friends remember? Friends.~
@219  = ~Can't you see I bring you the gift of oblivion? The bitterness of death is at hand!~ [cmca9]
@220  = ~What is this <CHARNAME>? I will not be in the same party as this filthy drow harlot. Come see me when you have decided to kill her or kick her out of your group. Perhaps after that, I may be persuaded to rejoin your motley group.~
@221  = ~What is this <CHARNAME>? I will not be in the same party as this filthy drow. Come see me when you have decided to kill him or kick him out of your group. Perhaps I may be persuaded to rejoin you.~
@222  = ~<CHARNAME>, if you let this drow whore in our group I'll leave!~
@223  = ~Ha! Opps, someone killed her dearest Uncle Quayle by mistake.~
@224  = ~I haven't felt this happy in a long time!~
@225  = ~Revenge must be served if you ask me. Oh yes sweet, sweet revenge!~
@226  = ~Yay! Another uppity self rightous knight. Oh how I hate them!~
@227  = ~How nice, we get to deal with these tree huggers. I'd rather burn down the woods, which in turn, would kill these druids. Easier way to get the job done I think.~
@228  = ~Oh this will be pretty, painting the walls with your blood little mage!~
@229  = ~Go on read it already! I'm curious to see what it does.~
@230  = ~Why must these simpletons keep offering suggestions to me? I am aware of what I want to do, leave me be!~
@231  = ~We don't need this fool of a bard. Stay and be a good little doggie.~
@232  = ~Leaving her is your choice, <CHARNAME>. From what I've heard about her, she's an annoying brat.~
@233  = ~My, my, Jaheira, you look under the weather, a tad bit weak. Ms. High and Mighty not feeling like herself?~
@234  = ~(Cough) I-I have more than enough strength to take on Ployer or you if this discussion continues.~
@235  = ~It would be a mistake to betray us, betray me, Jaheira.~
@236  = ~Let them get what they deserve. That wench shouldn't have cheated on you, Keldorn.~
@237  = ~It's about time to. This tomb is becoming quite a bore.~
@238  = ~Fear not girlie, I think it be gettin exciting right quick.~
@239  = ~If this sphere has anything of value in it, I could care less if your body is dead or alive, just as long as we get in.~
@240  = ~Betrayed? You filthy little worm! Come here and let me chop you into pieces!~
@241  = ~Ah, a discount. You should accept this and work for her, <CHARNAME>.~
@242  = ~Ah you wish to die slowly, hmmm?~
@243  = ~Out of the way tramp!~
@244  = ~Now this is my kind of entertainment! I love a good blood sport!~
@245  = ~Will you shut it you pompous ass! Your blue blood means nothing to me.~
@246  = ~Well I never! Common street trash whom dares to come into my home? Oh where our my guards when I need them?~
@247  = ~Ah yes I like this, watching these dumb animals fight. What is really interesting is watching the animals tear into people. Maul them until there is nothing left but bloody chunks. Ha ha!~
@248  = ~H-how horrible! You're a nasty e-evil woman, Callisto!~
@249  = ~Hey, <CHARNAME>, I suggest we throw the wingless wonder in there. I would love to see her fight a lion.~
@250  = ~You are weak for letting them steal from you. Stay and rot with your filthy fish.~
@251  = ~Ahhh p-please don't hurt me!~
@252  = ~Get out of my sight you weakling!~
@253  = ~My, my so many choices you have! But my choice is to kill you, you foul smelling mongrel!~
@254  = ~We shall see!~
@255  = ~Trotting off into the sewers is beneath us, <CHARNAME>. Why do we always have to help out these worthless priests all the time?~
@256  = ~Revenge. So sweet, so bitter, so cold.~
@257  = ~Such a sad story, <CHARNAME>. For a fair amount of coin I am sure we can make sure "justice" is served.~
@258  = ~We'll see how superior he is when my blade is stuck in him!~
@259  = ~On second thought, this is Nalia we are talking about. Do we really need to rescue that whiney wench?~
@260  = ~Well, I can see why he would object, you're a weak male.~
@261  = ~Keep the insults to yourself or feel my sword burn in your guts fool!~
@262  = ~Silence lout! I am speaking to <CHARNAME>, not you.~
@263  = ~A forgotten god? How amusing <CHARNAME>.~
@264  = ~Perhaps he should stay forgotten. Gods are worthless to begin with, <CHARNAME>, why help one who is forgotten?~
@265  = ~Such hatred I feel from them.~
@266  = ~It feels so refreshing for once, don't ya think?~
@267  = ~A good god is a dead god. Stay forgotten and die! Ha ha!~
@268  = ~I like the idea of stealing from these damnable priests, <CHARNAME>! Priests and their damned false gods! It would be better to burn their temple down, but stealing from it, that will satisfy just the same.~
@269  = ~Stealing? As long as it brings a lot of coin I have no objection to this.~
@270  = ~I like the idea of spilling the blood of a traitor or a betrayer, <CHARNAME>. But come to think of it, I like spilling blood regardless. He he!~
@271  = ~A good tactic to follow. A two front war is near impossible to win.~
@272  = ~Collecting coin is always good, <CHARNAME>. Killing Mae'Var is something I would do out of pure pleasure even if we didn't get paid for it!~
@273  = ~Your very own thief guild, <CHARNAME>. Rule them with a iron fist so they stay in line and know who their master is.~
@274  = ~Such a foolish wench you are. Let me be the first to draw her blood, <CHARNAME>!~
@275  = ~Open your eyes fool, we are not the guards. Taking your gold will do, but taking your lives is far, far better!~
@276  = ~What? Drow! Kill it quickly, <CHARNAME> before it takes action against us!~
@277  = ~Stay your blade surface elf and let me speak before you regret stepping foot in my domain.~
@278  = ~<CHARNAME> think about it. If this mage will offer us a great amount of coin, should we not accept his deal?~
@279  = ~Well, <CHARNAME>, if the townspeople are suspicious of outsiders, I will try to stay out of trouble and not draw attention to us.~
@280  = ~So we've been double-crossed? I hope you enjoy pain, because I'm going to bleed you nice and slow.~
@281  = ~Allies? You have to be joking fool! I say we go straight to the Underdark, <CHARNAME>. But before we go, let me draw and quarter him first.~
@282  = ~An excellent choice, <CHARNAME>. Morals? What's that?~
@283  = ~Get out of my face male, before I remove yours with my whip!~
@284  = ~I am surprised! I didn't think you had it in you, <CHARNAME>!~
@285  = ~AMUSING. NOW WHAT DO YOU PROPOSE?~
@286  = ~(Callisto smiles after you give Phaere the eggs. It's a look of satisfaction, knowing what will happen to Phaere and the "real" eggs.)~
@287  = ~A silver dragon in our midst. Can't say I'm impressed. Hmmm. I wonder how much I could get for the scale?~
@288  = ~Arrgghhh! I look like a filthy drow!.~
@289  = ~(She thinks for a moment.) As long as it's not permanent and our goal is reached, I'll have no problem with this. For now.~
@290  = ~(Callisto smiles, but the hate in her eyes reveal her true feelings.) Heh!~
@291  = ~Oh I will enjoy carving you up drow! A good drow is a dead drow! A bloody and beaten dead drow!!~
@292  = ~Why Anomen, I'm impressed! Tinhead has killed in cold blood. That was so "noble" of you, Anomen.~
@293  = ~How fascinating, <CHARNAME>!~
@294  = ~This thing, this awesome power, is what you carry in your soul?~
@295  = ~I really don't want to hear this right now, Callisto.~
@296  = ~Shut up, Callisto. I could care less about your interest in this.~
@297  = ~Its an evil thing that I wish no part of. The very essence of the Lord of Murder within me, how foul.~
@298  = ~Yes it is power, something I embrace.~
@299  = ~Oh? Very well!~
@300  = ~So be it.~
@301  = ~Really? I would embrace it whole heartedly!~
@302  = ~Now that's the spirit, <CHARNAME>, embrace it oh yes, feel the power!.~
@303  = ~Well, well what do we have here? A fine looking lass who shakes her hips, oh so inviting.~
@304  = ~Would you like to die, painfully?~
@305  = ~To die between your legs would be blissful.~
@306  = ~You should be careful for what you ask for little man.~
@307  = ~Shall I get a room for the both of us so you can show me the strength of those sexy legs?~
@308  = ~Oh no, no my little pet you're mistaken. You will die slowly and painfully. First thing to happen to you is castration. I will slowly cut those nasty organs off you and shove them down your throat. Next you'll be disemboweled and I will palce your entrails next to you. Shall I go on?~
@309  = ~Uhhh.~
@310  = ~If you are still alive after this, I will hack off your limbs and leave you as is, slowly bleeding to death.~
@311  = ~Oh my! Time sure does fly fast. One more drink and I better head for home. Mumsy is expecting me home for dinner at any moment.~
@312  = ~(Callisto stares at him expressionless except her eyes show her true feelings. Controlled rage is burning inside her, waiting to be released.)~
@313  = ~What is this? Another foul elf in my sight? You should all be exterminated like the vermin you are! My family died because of your kind!~
@314  = ~Ohh poor baby! Did you happen to find them crucified with this rune carved into their foreheads? (Callisto roles up her sleeve revealing a tattoo of a sword and snake entwined, with her initials around it.)~
@315  = ~W-what? How did you know this?~
@316  = ~No wonder your village was easily taken if they had fools like you who can't put two and two together. My army laid waste to your village and all survivors were killed, slowly. Would you like me to give you more details? It was a very good day!~
@317  = ~(His body shakes with rage.)~
@318  = ~Ha ha! It was a beautiful day for a blood bath. You should have been there! You could have heard your wife pleading for a mercy kill as she was slowly cut and bled. Next the bones in her limbs were shattered by the hammer. When the pain became too unbearable, she cursed your name for not being there to protect her.~
@319  = ~Y-you elven whore! I'll have my revenge!!~
@320  = ~Hey there! Good looking blond!~
@321  = ~What do you want little man?~
@322  = ~See this lovely sphere behind me? It can be all yours for the small of 500 gold pieces! No better bargain in Athkatla!~
@323  = ~What would I want with this? I never stay at any one place for too long.~
@324  = ~Well if could be a good permanent place to stay for you and ...~
@325  = ~It could be your permanent resting place if you keep pushing it. Now stop bothering me.~
@326  = ~Hey pretty lady can I play with your sword?~
@327  = ~Go away little one if you wish to grow up and be old.~ [cmca39]
@328  = ~Ahhhh!~
@329  = ~You sure are pretty looking except for that ugly scar on the side of yer face.~
@330  = ~You want one?~
@331  = ~Ahh mommy!~
@332  = ~Are you a fighter lady? You sure look like one.~
@333  = ~What if I was?~
@334  = ~I want to see you fight.~
@335  = ~What if I small your skull in? Now that is something I want to see!~
@336  = ~Run, run! Devil lady!~
@337  = ~What ya doin 'round 'ere?~
@338  = ~Looking for fools to practice my sword on.~
@339  = ~What ya lookin at? Shouldn't ya be whorin some where else?~
@340  = ~I thought I would clean the streets of the trash that walks it.~
@341  = ~Er now I was jus kiddin, meant no 'arm.~
@342  = ~Eh Callisto? What are ye doin here?~
@343  = ~A little bit of ale, partying or sleep, I can't decide.~
@344  = ~I would recommend sleep. The last time ye were 'ere ye nearly trashed the place.~
@345  = ~It was a celebration what did you expect?~
@346  = ~Well try and behave yer self this time or I'll call the guard.~
@347  = ~We'll see, no promises though.~
